          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How should I store emergency lanterns?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Keep them somewhere cool, dry and easy to find in the dark, with at least one on every floor. Charge rechargeable lanterns and test battery lanterns twice a year, and store alkaline cells outside the light to prevent leaks. A spare set of batteries taped to or stored beside each lantern removes the guesswork when the power goes out."
