            A few patterns stand out. Only the rechargeable lanterns offer USB output, which turns them into small emergency phone chargers; that is a meaningful bonus but should not be your main phone-charging plan, since every watt that goes to the phone comes out of your light. The disposable-battery lights trade convenience for shelf life, which is why they belong in the kit as backups rather than as the primary light. And the brightest light on the list is a headlamp, which is a reminder that a focused beam is a different tool from a room light.
          </p>

